## ESP32 Boot Spike — Phase 1 test script
## Tests that the ESP32 platform definition loads and Xtensa CPU executes instructions.
##
## Usage:
##   mono /Applications/Renode.app/Contents/MacOS/bin/Renode.exe scripts/esp32-boot-test.resc
##
## This script loads the Zephyr hello-world sample compiled for Xtensa sample_controller
## to verify basic CPU execution. The ESP32 platform memory regions overlap with the
## sample_controller layout, so the binary should execute.

using sysbus

# Create the ESP32 machine
mach create "esp32"
machine LoadPlatformDescription @platforms/meadow-esp32.repl

# Show UART output
showAnalyzer uart0
showAnalyzer cpu.uartSemihosting

# Load Zephyr hello-world for Xtensa (uses semihosting UART, so output goes to uartSemihosting)
# This validates that the Xtensa CPU with esp32 cpuType can execute code.
macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF @https://dl.antmicro.com/projects/renode/xtensa-sample-controller-zephyr-hello-world.elf-s_293544-4be60f8a3891e70c30e1e8a471df4ad12ab08144
"""
runMacro $reset
